hierarchy_code,channel,year,week_num,units,discount_perc
# OPTIONAL FILE. Rename to sales_history.csv to activate. One row per
# SKU x channel x ABSOLUTE-YEAR x fiscal-week.
#
# `year` is the real calendar year (e.g. 2024, 2025, 2026) — NOT a relative
# TY/LY/LLY label. The tool maps the year you SELECT (Y) to TY=Y, LY=Y-1,
# LLY=Y-2, and for each comparison year pulls a week from this file when it is
# ALREADY ACTUALISED, otherwise from that year's WP forecast.
#
# So put your ACTUALS here, by the year they happened:
#   - fully-past years  → all 52 weeks
#   - the current year  → only the weeks already closed (e.g. 1..19 if "now" is wk20)
#   - future years      → omit (no actuals yet; the WP forecast fills them)
#
# A stream (hc+channel) listed here plans on its own history; forward weeks are
# reforecast from the most recent FULL prior year's shape. A SKU NOT listed here
# keeps the parametric peak_week/peak_units curve.
# week_num is the fiscal week 1..52 (not the 6-digit week_code). units >= 0.
# discount_perc is a fraction (0.10 = 10% off); leave blank for 0.
# Example: SKU 10001 Ecom — 2024 + 2025 full actuals, 2026 actuals through wk3.
